# Zot repositories

## Gate

Use when the user authorized Zot work and the turn needs **repository**
inventory: list repos, pick a repo for tags/referrers, or audit registry
shape. Skip bare "OCI registry" talk without Zot. Load `zot-safety` on
every Zot turn. Tags/manifests/referrers → `zot-tags`. Other OCI registry
products are out of scope.

## Prefer live surface

No Zot MCP was discovered in the live harness catalog. Prefer:

1. Zot **API** / Distribution-compatible endpoints with a base URL from
   operator config / env
2. Authenticated Zot **UI** when API access is unavailable

If an MCP appears later, discover tools from the live map — do not invent
tool names. Never hardcode a host. Never invent repository names —
list/resolve this turn or use exact names the user pasted.

## Craft

| Need | Approach |
| --- | --- |
| List repositories | Catalog/list API or UI Repositories |
| One repository | Resolve from list; report name + tag count when present |
| Auth / anonymous pull policy | Read-only note — changes need `zot-safety` |

## Discover first

1. Resolve **base URL** from config/env — refuse guessing.
2. List repositories before naming one for tag or GC work.
3. Report **repo name** — never paste htpasswd / token secrets.

## Procedure (read paths)

1. **Scope** — fleet list vs one named repo. **Done when** clear.
2. **List / resolve** — evidence from API/UI this turn.
   **Done when** every repo name you cite was listed or user-pasted.
3. **Report** — short table (see shape). **Done when** no secrets appear.

## Report shape

- **repository**
- **tags** — count when available
- **base URL** — product host only; no credentials

## Out of scope

- Tag/manifest/referrer detail → `zot-tags`
- Delete tag/repo / GC / auth mutate → `zot-safety`
- Other OCI registries

## Related (this plugin)

- `zot-tags` — tags, manifests, referrers
- `zot-safety` — delete / GC / auth gates
